---
// TASK 2.2.4: the first page behind a session. Statically generated and
// **empty** — ADR-0017's static-output decision is intact, because what
// makes this page private is not server rendering but that its content is
// not in the HTML at all. The islands below decide whether to build any,
// and render nothing until the session resolves.
//
// ## 2026-09-06: for a patient, this page *is* the account
//
// The owner: *"the moment a patient signs in it lands to his dashboard.
// This dashboard has 'My calender', 'Personal Details', 'Testimonial' and
// 'Account' section. Inside 'My Calender' we already have a nice looking
// calender. Inside 'Personal Details' keep all personal details option,
// inside 'Testimonial' keep testimonial content and inside 'Account' have
// option to change password."*
//
// Until now this page was a **menu**: a list of links to `account/patient`,
// `account/appointments`, `account/testimonial` and
// `account/change-password`, plus a notifications feed. A patient signing in
// landed on a page whose entire content was directions to four other pages.
// Now the four pages' content is here, in four named sections, and the
// pages themselves remain — reachable by URL, still registered in
// `account-routes.ts` for the authenticated a11y gate, and still the place
// a deep link lands. What is gone is the layer of links in between.
//
// Two things went with it, at the owner's word — *"remove Updates section
// and My Calender button on dashboard as they are redundant"*:
//
//   * `PatientNotifications` ("Updates"). Its feed is appointment-approved
//     / appointment-cancelled / calendar-updated notices — every one of them
//     a statement about a slot the calendar directly above now shows.
//   * The "My calendar" link, for the same reason twice over: it pointed at
//     `account/appointments`, a forward-only list of the appointments the
//     calendar already draws.
//
// `account.signedInIntro` went too — "your care plan and appointments will
// appear here" was a promise printed directly above the thing it promised.
//
// ## 2026-09-06, second pass: the staff half gets the same treatment
//
// *"in clinician account, i seeing my calander button (this is redundant
// now). Remove it … have an account section to reset password just like you
// did for patient."*
//
// The "My calendar" link pointed at `account/calendar` — a forward-looking
// 30-day list of the appointments the calendar at the top of this page
// already draws, for the same roles. Gone for the same reason the patient's
// own calendar link went.
//
// The change-password link is replaced by an inlined **Account** section, and
// it carries both of that page's panels rather than only the password form:
// `OwnDetailsPanel` is where a clinician sets their display name, and
// inlining half the page would have left the other half reachable by typed
// URL alone.
//
// What is left in the staff shell is genuinely a list of *other* places —
// the caseload, patient administration, clinician administration, authoring
// — none of which is a panel this page could reasonably absorb.
//
// ## 2026-09-07: the patient half is renamed to the record's own four areas
//
// The owner: *"for patient it will be Patient Details, Patient Assessment
// Form, Patient Prescription, Patient Appointments, Patient Account and
// Patient Testimonial."*
//
// Four of those six are the areas of the patient record itself, and they
// are the same four `patient-record.astro` now shows staff — so a patient
// and their clinician are looking at areas with the same names, which they
// were not before ("Personal details" here, "Details" there, one unnamed
// run of form sections under both). The remaining two are this page's own
// and stay exactly as they were, renamed: "Account" is the password form,
// "Testimonial" the testimonial panel.
//
// **"Patient Assessment Form" is not among the five a patient sees**, and
// that is the owner's own rule from the same message: *"Patient Assessment
// will only be visible to clinician and principal clinician."* It is
// `private{}`, denied to a patient in every cell since 2026-09-01. No
// placement for it is mounted here — a heading over a section the server
// answers with nothing would announce the existence of notes written about
// them, which is the one thing R-09 is careful never to do.
//
// **Section order is the owner's**, given twice on 2026-09-07 and settled
// by the second: *"for patient dashboard, I want the content to be in this
// order - at the top Calender, then Patient Details, Patient Prescriptions,
// Patient Account, and Patient Testimonial."*
//
// So the calendar is back at the very top, where 2026-09-06 put it — the
// first list read as Details-first and moved it down, and it was wrong for
// half a day. The area keeps its "Patient Appointments" heading rather than
// becoming "Calendar": that is the name the owner gave it in the message
// before, it is what staff see on `patient-record.astro`, and the second
// instruction is about *where the content sits*, not what it is called.
import { supportedLocales, t } from '@ndn/i18n';
import type { Locale } from '@ndn/i18n';
import { Heading, Link } from '@ndn/ui';

import { AppointmentCalendar } from '../../../account/AppointmentCalendar.js';
import { AssessmentForm } from '../../../account/AssessmentForm.js';
import { appointmentCalendarStylesCss } from '../../../account/calendar-styles.js';
import { caseloadStylesCss } from '../../../account/caseload-styles.js';
import { CaseloadView } from '../../../account/CaseloadView.js';
import { ChangePasswordPanel } from '../../../account/ChangePasswordPanel.js';
import { accountDashboardStylesCss } from '../../../account/dashboard-styles.js';
import { NextAppointmentLead } from '../../../account/NextAppointmentLead.js';
import { OwnDetailsPanel } from '../../../account/OwnDetailsPanel.js';
import { PatientProfile } from '../../../account/PatientProfile.js';
import { patientRecordStylesCss } from '../../../account/record-styles.js';
import { TestimonialPanel } from '../../../account/TestimonialPanel.js';
import { RequireAuth } from '../../../auth/RequireAuth.js';
import { SignInLink } from '../../../auth/SignInPanel.js';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteName } from '../../../site-config.js';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return supportedLocales.map((locale) => ({ params: { locale } }));
}

const { locale } = Astro.params as { locale: Locale };
const heading = t('account.heading', undefined, locale);

/**
 * Every panel gathered into a named section renders its own heading one
 * level down, so the outline reads "page > section > panel" rather than a
 * flat run of `<h2>`s. See `account/heading-level.ts`.
 */
const PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL = 3;

/**
 * The calendar is mounted twice on this page and exactly one of the two
 * ever renders — the role gates around them are disjoint. Staff get it at
 * the top of the dashboard, where 2026-09-06 put it; a patient gets it
 * inside their "Patient Appointments" section, where 2026-09-07's ordering
 * puts it. One string bag, so the two placements cannot drift into
 * describing the same control differently.
 */
const calendarStrings = {
  heading: t('accountCalendar.heading', undefined, locale),
  loadingLabel: t('accountCalendar.loading', undefined, locale),
  forbiddenLabel: t('accountCalendar.forbidden', undefined, locale),
  errorLabel: t('accountCalendar.error', undefined, locale),
  // 2026-09-08: the two the stale-while-revalidate pass added. See the
  // component's header — a window move keeps the month it is leaving on
  // screen, so it needs a word for "a newer one is coming" and a word for
  // "it did not arrive" that are not the whole-view loading and error
  // strings above.
  refreshingLabel: t('accountCalendar.refreshing', undefined, locale),
  refreshFailedLabel: t('accountCalendar.refreshFailed', undefined, locale),
  previousWeeksLabel: t('accountCalendar.previousWeeks', undefined, locale),
  nextWeeksLabel: t('accountCalendar.nextWeeks', undefined, locale),
  todayLabel: t('accountCalendar.today', undefined, locale),
  gridCaption: t('accountCalendar.gridCaption', undefined, locale),
  todayMarker: t('accountCalendar.todayMarker', undefined, locale),
  noAppointmentsOnDay: t('accountCalendar.noAppointmentsOnDay', undefined, locale),
  emptyWindow: t('accountCalendar.emptyWindow', undefined, locale),
  durationLabel: t('accountCalendar.duration', undefined, locale),
  minutesSuffix: t('patientRecord.minutesSuffix', undefined, locale),
  statusLabel: t('accountCalendar.status', undefined, locale),
  patientLabel: t('accountCalendar.patient', undefined, locale),
  clinicianLabel: t('accountCalendar.clinician', undefined, locale),
  joinCallLabel: t('calendar.joinCall', undefined, locale),
  // The four decisions inherited from the deleted `account/calendar`
  // page, reusing its own catalogue entries rather than new copy.
  approveLabel: t('clinicianCalendar.approve', undefined, locale),
  declineLabel: t('clinicianCalendar.decline', undefined, locale),
  completeLabel: t('clinicianCalendar.complete', undefined, locale),
  noShowLabel: t('clinicianCalendar.noShow', undefined, locale),
  decidingLabel: t('clinicianCalendar.deciding', undefined, locale),
  decideFailedLabel: t('clinicianCalendar.decideFailed', undefined, locale),
  statusLabels: {
    // Keyed by the API's own `appointment_status` values
    // (`packages/shared-types/src/appointment.ts`), so an
    // unrecognised one falls through to the raw value rather than
    // rendering blank.
    scheduled: t('accountCalendar.status.scheduled', undefined, locale),
    'pending-approval': t('accountCalendar.status.pendingApproval', undefined, locale),
    completed: t('accountCalendar.status.completed', undefined, locale),
    cancelled: t('accountCalendar.status.cancelled', undefined, locale),
    'no-show': t('accountCalendar.status.noShow', undefined, locale),
  },
};

/**
 * Three placements of the assessment form on a patient's dashboard, one per
 * area of the record they may read. Built once for the same reason the
 * calendar's is — and note there is no fourth: `private{}` has no placement
 * here at all. See this page's header.
 */
const assessmentStrings = {
  heading: t('assessment.heading', undefined, locale),
  loadingLabel: t('assessment.loading', undefined, locale),
  forbiddenLabel: t('assessment.forbidden', undefined, locale),
  notFoundLabel: t('assessment.notFound', undefined, locale),
  errorLabel: t('assessment.error', undefined, locale),
  missingIdLabel: t('assessment.missingId', undefined, locale),
  saveLabel: t('assessment.save', undefined, locale),
  savingLabel: t('assessment.saving', undefined, locale),
  savedLabel: t('assessment.saved', undefined, locale),
  autosavedLabel: t('assessment.autosaved', undefined, locale),
  conflictLabel: t('assessment.conflict', undefined, locale),
  saveForbiddenLabel: t('assessment.saveForbidden', undefined, locale),
  readOnlyLabel: t('assessment.readOnly', undefined, locale),
  attachmentsHeading: t('assessment.attachmentsHeading', undefined, locale),
  attachmentsEmpty: t('assessment.attachmentsEmpty', undefined, locale),
  addFileLabel: t('assessment.addFile', undefined, locale),
  uploadingLabel: t('assessment.uploading', undefined, locale),
  uploadFailedLabel: t('assessment.uploadFailed', undefined, locale),
  downloadLabel: t('assessment.download', undefined, locale),
  uploadedAtTemplate: t('assessment.uploadedAt', { when: '{when}' }, locale),
  addRowLabel: t('assessment.addRow', undefined, locale),
  removeRowLabel: t('assessment.removeRow', undefined, locale),
  addRowAriaTemplate: t('assessment.addRowAria', { field: '{field}' }, locale),
  removeRowAriaTemplate: t('assessment.removeRowAria', { row: '{row}', field: '{field}' }, locale),
  cellLabelTemplate: t('assessment.cellLabel', { field: '{field}', column: '{column}', row: '{row}' }, locale),
  noNextAppointmentLabel: t('assessment.noNextAppointment', undefined, locale),
  versionLabel: t('assessment.version', undefined, locale),
};

/** The password form's copy — the same panel serves the patient's "Patient Account" section and the staff "Account" one. */
const changePasswordStrings = {
  heading: t('changePassword.heading', undefined, locale),
  intro: t('changePassword.intro', undefined, locale),
  currentPasswordLabel: t('changePassword.currentPasswordLabel', undefined, locale),
  newPasswordLabel: t('changePassword.newPasswordLabel', undefined, locale),
  confirmPasswordLabel: t('changePassword.confirmPasswordLabel', undefined, locale),
  submitButton: t('changePassword.submitButton', undefined, locale),
  submitting: t('changePassword.submitting', undefined, locale),
  successMessage: t('changePassword.successMessage', undefined, locale),
  mismatchError: t('changePassword.mismatchError', undefined, locale),
  forbidden: t('changePassword.forbidden', undefined, locale),
  incorrectCurrentPasswordError: t(
    'changePassword.incorrectCurrentPasswordError',
    undefined,
    locale,
  ),
  policyViolationError: t('changePassword.policyViolationError', undefined, locale),
  error: t('changePassword.error', undefined, locale),
};
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  title={`${heading} — ${siteName}`}
  description={t('account.description', undefined, locale)}
>
  <Heading level={1}>{heading}</Heading>

  <RequireAuth client:only="react" loadingLabel={t('account.loading', undefined, locale)}>
    <Fragment slot="signedOut">
      <p>
        {t('account.signedOut', undefined, locale)}{' '}
        <SignInLink label={t('account.signInPatient', undefined, locale)} pool="patient" />
        {' · '}
        <SignInLink label={t('account.signInClinician', undefined, locale)} pool="clinician" />
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    {/* ## Staff: the calendar, at the top of the dashboard.
        2026-09-06: *"At the very top I want to show calender … where the
        patient/clinician/principal clinician can scroll left and right to
        see all past and upcoming appointments. There is no concept of
        calender for help desk and visitor."*

        **Helpdesk joined them on 2026-09-06**: *"for help desk I want to
        show on the landing dashboard both ready only calender and patient
        dashboard — the two stuff the principal clinician is seeing but in
        read only mode."* They read the same island; the server answers a
        helpdesk with the practice's calendar rather than their own empty
        one, and `mayActOnAppointments` is what makes it read-only, so
        nothing here needs a second set of props. Only **visitor** is left
        outside now, which is the half of the original instruction nobody
        has questioned.

        **2026-09-07: this placement is staff-only, and a patient's own
        calendar moved down** into their "Patient Appointments" section — the
        owner's new ordering puts Details and Prescription above it. Two
        placements of one component, and the role gates are disjoint, so
        exactly one of them ever renders in a session.

        The component refuses a visitor as well (`calendarSourcesFor`), so it
        is safe wherever it is mounted — but the gate here means a visitor
        session never downloads the island at all. No `forbidden` slot: a
        role with no calendar should see no trace of one, not an explanation
        of its absence. The section heading is the component's own. */}
    {/* 2026-09-10: the next appointment above the calendar, as the patient
        already has it. The owner: *"for clinician landing dashboard, show the
        next appointment above My Calender just like how it's being shown for
        patient."*

        `NextAppointmentLead` (`audience="clinician"`) derives the same figure
        the patient's own lead shows — the three zoned times and the live
        countdown of `NextAppointmentWhen` — from the calendar the clinician
        already reads (`GET /clinicians/me/calendar`), since a clinician has no
        assessment record to carry a `calendarSummary`, and names the patient
        the appointment is with. It shares the calendar's own three-role gate:
        for a helpdesk the server answers "me" with the practice's calendar, so
        their lead is the practice's next appointment, matching the calendar
        directly below it — with the patient name withheld, the same two facts
        a patient's own box shows. It renders nothing until its own fetch
        lands, so it never paints an empty box above the calendar.

        **2026-09-10, second pass: the staff calendar is a sheet now, like the
        patient's.** The owner, comparing the two dashboards: *"that green
        heading is missing almost entirely in clinician landing dashboard.
        Make it follow exactly the same style as happening in patients
        profile."* A patient's calendar lives inside a `ndn-record-area` sheet
        under a tinted "Patient Appointments" band; the staff one floated bare
        on the page ground. It now carries the same wrapper and band — the
        lead and the calendar sit inside it exactly as they do for a patient.
        The band's own title is "Appointments" (the patient's is "Patient
        Appointments"), and the calendar keeps its own "My calendar" heading
        inside, the same two-heading shape the patient reads. */}
    <RequireAuth
      client:only="react"
      allowRoles={['principal-clinician', 'sub-clinician', 'helpdesk']}
    >
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="clinician-appointments-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="clinician-appointments-heading">
          {t('account.section.appointments', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <NextAppointmentLead
          client:only="react"
          audience="clinician"
          locale={locale}
          strings={{
            appointmentLabel: t('nextAppointmentLead.appointmentLabel', undefined, locale),
            durationLabel: t('nextAppointmentLead.durationLabel', undefined, locale),
            personLabel: t('nextAppointmentLead.patientLabel', undefined, locale),
            emptyLabel: t('assessment.noNextAppointment', undefined, locale),
          }}
        />
        <AppointmentCalendar client:only="react" locale={locale} strings={calendarStrings} />
      </section>
    </RequireAuth>

    {/* ## 1a. Patient dashboard — the caseload table itself, not a link to it.
        *"there is still a button to be clicked for patient dashboard for
        clinicians account. rather keep that table that otherwise opens when
        we click that button on the landing dashboard itself."*

        `account/caseload` is deleted; the table it existed to mount is here.
        The four roles are that page's own `allowRoles` — the table renders
        different columns for a visitor (name, address, appointment count)
        than for a clinician, which `CaseloadView` decides from the resolved
        role rather than from anything passed here.

        The one thing that had to move with it is `patient-record`'s "back to
        dashboard" link, which pointed at the deleted page and now points
        here — where the table it means actually is.

        **2026-09-06: directly beneath the calendar, not at the foot of the
        page.** The owner: *"for clinician and principal clinician on logged
        in landing dashboard immediately after calender have patient
        dashboard. atm, it's at the bottom."* It had been sitting below the
        staff Account section — a password form standing between a clinician
        and their own caseload, which is the thing they actually signed in
        to work from. The two sections a clinician sees are now ordered by
        how often they are wanted rather than by the order they were built.

        It sits *between* the numbered patient sections and does not disturb
        them: everything from "## 2" down is gated to `patient`, and this is
        gated to the four staff roles, so no session ever renders both. */}
    <RequireAuth
      client:only="react"
      allowRoles={['principal-clinician', 'sub-clinician', 'helpdesk', 'visitor']}
    >
      {/* 2026-09-10: the same `ndn-record-area` sheet the patient's sections
          carry — the owner wanted the staff dashboard to *"follow exactly the
          same style as happening in patients profile"*, and a bare section
          under a floating heading was the odd one out. The band now reads
          "Patient dashboard" over the caseload the way "Patient Appointments"
          reads over the calendar above it. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="caseload-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="caseload-heading">
          {t('account.dashboardLink', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <CaseloadView
          client:only="react"
          recordHrefBase={`/${locale}/account/patient-record`}
          strings={{
            loadingLabel: t('caseload.loading', undefined, locale),
            forbiddenLabel: t('caseload.forbidden', undefined, locale),
            errorLabel: t('caseload.error', undefined, locale),
            emptyLabel: t('caseload.empty', undefined, locale),
            patientColumnLabel: t('caseload.patientColumn', undefined, locale),
            statusColumnLabel: t('caseload.statusColumn', undefined, locale),
            clinicianColumnLabel: t('caseload.clinicianColumn', undefined, locale),
            assignColumnLabel: t('caseload.assignColumn', undefined, locale),
            nextPageLabel: t('caseload.nextPage', undefined, locale),
            previousPageLabel: t('caseload.previousPage', undefined, locale),
            // Not the page heading repeated — a caption's job is to say what
            // the table contains, and the owner's own reason for wanting this
            // table is the sentence it now carries.
            caption: t('caseload.tableCaption', undefined, locale),
            pagerLabel: t('caseload.pagerLabel', undefined, locale),
            totalPatientsLabel: t('caseload.totalPatients', undefined, locale),
            activePatientsLabel: t('caseload.activePatients', undefined, locale),
            statusPendingLabel: t('caseload.statusPending', undefined, locale),
            statusApprovedLabel: t('caseload.statusApproved', undefined, locale),
            statusDeclinedLabel: t('caseload.statusDeclined', undefined, locale),
            statusSuspendedLabel: t('caseload.statusSuspended', undefined, locale),
            unassignedLabel: t('caseload.unassigned', undefined, locale),
            chooseClinicianLabel: t('caseload.chooseClinician', undefined, locale),
            assignButton: t('caseload.assignButton', undefined, locale),
            reassignButton: t('caseload.reassignButton', undefined, locale),
            working: t('caseload.working', undefined, locale),
            assignError: t('caseload.assignError', undefined, locale),
            noCliniciansLabel: t('caseload.noClinicians', undefined, locale),
            openRecordLabel: t('caseload.openRecord', undefined, locale),
            removeColumnLabel: t('caseload.removeColumn', undefined, locale),
            suspendButton: t('caseload.suspendButton', undefined, locale),
            restoreButton: t('caseload.restoreButton', undefined, locale),
            suspendConfirm: t('caseload.suspendConfirm', undefined, locale),
            statusError: t('caseload.statusError', undefined, locale),
            addressColumnLabel: t('caseload.addressColumn', undefined, locale),
            appointmentsColumnLabel: t('caseload.appointmentsColumn', undefined, locale),
          }}
        />
      </section>
    </RequireAuth>

    {/* The patient's five sections, in the owner's own order — revised
        2026-09-07, second pass: *"for patient dashboard, I want the content
        to be in this order - at the top Calender, then Patient Details,
        Patient Prescriptions, Patient Account, and Patient Testimonial."*

        The calendar goes back to the top, where 2026-09-06 first put it
        (*"At the very top I want to show calender"*) and where a patient's
        own screen had it until earlier today. It keeps the "Patient
        Appointments" heading — the area name from the same owner's previous
        message, and the one `patient-record.astro` shows staff — so the
        instruction moved the section rather than renaming it.

        Everything from here to the staff Account block is gated to
        `patient`, and the staff blocks above and below are gated to the
        other roles, so no session ever renders both. */}
    <RequireAuth client:only="react" allowRoles={['patient']}>
      {/* ## 1. Patient Appointments — the calendar (*"Inside 'My Calender'
          we already have a nice looking calender"*), with the record's own
          `calendar{}` figures around it. Both are read-only for a patient.

          A second placement of `AppointmentCalendar`; the staff one above is
          gated to the three staff roles and this to `patient`, so exactly
          one of the two ever renders.

          **2026-09-09: the section's own figures now sit on both sides of
          the calendar**, at the owner's word: *"move 'Next appointment' and
          'Next appointment length (minutes)' above the 'My Calender' with
          slightly bigger font (subtly highlighted) so that that's what the
          patient sees first before checking the actual calender."*

          The **lower** figures are still a `calendar{}` placement of
          `AssessmentForm`, mounted with `hideFields` naming the two lead
          fields and the three the same message cut (*"I dont want 'Files',
          'Scheduling notes', 'Appointments awaiting the principal
          clinician’s approval'"*). A placement filter over what the server
          sent, so nothing here changes what a *clinician* sees on
          `patient-record.astro`: they still write the scheduling notes and
          still attach files to this section. It keeps the appointment totals
          and the section's "you can read this but not change it" note.

          **2026-09-11: the lead is `NextAppointmentLead`, not an
          `AssessmentForm` placement.** The owner: *"on patient's landing
          dashboard … also show the name of the clinician with whom he will
          have appointment with."* That name is not in the record's
          `calendarSummary` — the derived figures the form reads — so the box
          could not have carried it. The same component the clinician's box
          uses reads the patient's own appointments (`GET
          /patients/me/appointments`, the endpoint the calendar below already
          reads) and names the clinician off the next one; `audience` is the
          only thing that differs between the two dashboards. The next
          appointment and its length are the same instant the old placement
          showed, computed the same way (`findNext`), and the "No appointment
          is booked yet" note comes with it. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="patient-appointments-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="patient-appointments-heading">
          {t('account.section.patientAppointments', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <NextAppointmentLead
          client:only="react"
          audience="patient"
          locale={locale}
          strings={{
            appointmentLabel: t('nextAppointmentLead.appointmentLabel', undefined, locale),
            durationLabel: t('nextAppointmentLead.durationLabel', undefined, locale),
            personLabel: t('nextAppointmentLead.clinicianLabel', undefined, locale),
            emptyLabel: t('assessment.noNextAppointment', undefined, locale),
          }}
        />
        <AppointmentCalendar client:only="react" locale={locale} strings={calendarStrings} />
        <AssessmentForm
          client:only="react"
          locale={locale}
          fieldSets={['calendar']}
          hideFields={[
            'nextAppointmentAt',
            'nextAppointmentDurationMinutes',
            'appointmentsAwaitingApproval',
            'schedulingNotes',
          ]}
          showAttachments={false}
          showTitles={false}
          showVersion={false}
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={assessmentStrings}
        />
      </section>

      {/* ## 2. Patient Details — the identity form, then the record's own
          `general{}` section. The same area name `patient-record.astro`
          gives staff, and the same two stores behind it.

          Three panels the owner cut on 2026-09-06 are still gone:
          `NextAppointmentPanel` (*"remove the next appointment panel too,
          its redundant"*) and both `ClinicalRecordTimeline`s (*"remove care
          plan and diagnosis plan as I dont know when I define these
          sections"*). They are unmounted, not deleted — the API and its
          history are untouched. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="patient-details-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="patient-details-heading">
          {t('account.section.patientDetails', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <PatientProfile
          client:only="react"
          strings={{
            loadingLabel: t('patientProfile.loading', undefined, locale),
            forbiddenLabel: t('patientProfile.forbidden', undefined, locale),
            errorLabel: t('patientProfile.error', undefined, locale),
            savedLabel: t('patientProfile.saved', undefined, locale),
            fullNameLabel: t('patientProfile.fullName', undefined, locale),
            emailLabel: t('patientProfile.email', undefined, locale),
            phoneLabel: t('patientProfile.phone', undefined, locale),
            saveLabel: t('patientProfile.save', undefined, locale),
            savingLabel: t('patientProfile.saving', undefined, locale),
          }}
        />
        {/* Resolves to the signed-in patient's own form (`me`), so no `?id=`
            is involved. `general{}` is the one section they may edit — and
            the `tag` field inside it is `staffOnly`, which the form greys
            out rather than offering an input the save would refuse. */}
        <AssessmentForm
          client:only="react"
          locale={locale}
          fieldSets={['general']}
          showTitles={false}
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={assessmentStrings}
        />
      </section>

      {/* ## 3. Patient Prescription — read-only for a patient
          (`prescription{}` grants them `R` and not `U`), which the form says
          in as many words rather than by offering disabled inputs. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="patient-prescription-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="patient-prescription-heading">
          {t('account.section.patientPrescription', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <AssessmentForm
          client:only="react"
          locale={locale}
          fieldSets={['prescription']}
          showTitles={false}
          showVersion={false}
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={assessmentStrings}
        />
      </section>

      {/* ## 4. Patient Account — the password form from
          `account/change-password`. Only the password form: that page also
          carries `OwnDetailsPanel`, which the API serves to *staff* (`GET
          /clinicians/me`) and refuses a patient, so inlining it here would
          render a permanent "you do not have access" panel on a patient's
          own dashboard. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="patient-account-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="patient-account-heading">
          {t('account.section.patientAccount', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <ChangePasswordPanel
          client:only="react"
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={changePasswordStrings}
        />
      </section>

      {/* ## 5. Patient Testimonial — `account/testimonial` inlined. The
          panel renders its own heading ("Your testimonial"), so it sits one
          level down inside this section like every other panel here. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="patient-testimonial-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="patient-testimonial-heading">
          {t('account.section.patientTestimonial', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <TestimonialPanel
          client:only="react"
          locale={locale}
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={{
            heading: t('accountTestimonial.panelHeading', undefined, locale),
            intro: t('accountTestimonial.intro', undefined, locale),
            loading: t('accountTestimonial.loading', undefined, locale),
            forbidden: t('accountTestimonial.forbidden', undefined, locale),
            unavailable: t('accountTestimonial.unavailable', undefined, locale),
            error: t('accountTestimonial.error', undefined, locale),
            quoteLabel: t('testimonials.form.quoteLabel', undefined, locale),
            displayLabel: t('testimonials.form.attributionDisplayLabel', undefined, locale),
            displayFull: t('testimonials.form.attributionDisplay.full', undefined, locale),
            displayFirstNameOnly: t(
              'testimonials.form.attributionDisplay.firstNameOnly',
              undefined,
              locale,
            ),
            displayAnonymous: t(
              'testimonials.form.attributionDisplay.anonymous',
              undefined,
              locale,
            ),
            nameLabel: t('testimonials.form.attributionNameLabel', undefined, locale),
            nameRequired: t('accountTestimonial.nameRequired', undefined, locale),
            consentNotice: t('accountTestimonial.consentNotice', undefined, locale),
            publishButton: t('accountTestimonial.publish', undefined, locale),
            updateButton: t('accountTestimonial.update', undefined, locale),
            saving: t('accountTestimonial.saving', undefined, locale),
            savedMessage: t('accountTestimonial.saved', undefined, locale),
            withdrawButton: t('accountTestimonial.withdraw', undefined, locale),
            withdrawnMessage: t('accountTestimonial.withdrawn', undefined, locale),
            withdrawnNotice: t('accountTestimonial.withdrawnNotice', undefined, locale),
            saveFailed: t('accountTestimonial.saveFailed', undefined, locale),
          }}
        />
      </section>
    </RequireAuth>

    {/* ## Account — the staff half of the same section the patient gets.
        *"have an account section to reset password just like you did for
        patient."*

        It carries **both** panels from `account/change-password`, not just
        the password form: `OwnDetailsPanel` is served by `GET /clinicians/me`
        and is where a clinician sets their own display name. Inlining only
        the password form would have left that reachable by typed URL alone,
        which is the exact problem this dashboard has spent three changes
        undoing. The link is gone because the page's whole content is here.

        Patients are excluded: `GET /clinicians/me` refuses them, so they
        would get a permanent "you do not have access" panel — and they have
        their own Account section above. */}
    <RequireAuth
      client:only="react"
      allowRoles={['principal-clinician', 'sub-clinician', 'helpdesk', 'visitor']}
    >
      {/* 2026-09-10: `ndn-record-area`, the same sheet the patient's own
          Account section carries. Without it this was a bare `<section>` — the
          heading and the two panels stacked on the page ground with default
          margins, which the owner saw as *"bad vertical spacing"*. The class
          is the whole difference: the sheet, the tinted heading band and the
          rhythm the patient's Account already reads with, and a two-island
          area (display name + password) is the same shape Patient Details
          already is. */}
      <section class="ndn-record-area" aria-labelledby="staff-account-heading">
        <Heading level={2} id="staff-account-heading">
          {t('account.accountSectionHeading', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <OwnDetailsPanel
          client:only="react"
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={{
            heading: t('ownDetails.heading', undefined, locale),
            intro: t('ownDetails.intro', undefined, locale),
            displayNameLabel: t('ownDetails.displayNameLabel', undefined, locale),
            saveButton: t('ownDetails.saveButton', undefined, locale),
            saving: t('ownDetails.saving', undefined, locale),
            savedMessage: t('ownDetails.savedMessage', undefined, locale),
            loading: t('ownDetails.loading', undefined, locale),
            forbidden: t('ownDetails.forbidden', undefined, locale),
            error: t('ownDetails.error', undefined, locale),
          }}
        />
        <ChangePasswordPanel
          client:only="react"
          headingLevel={PANEL_HEADING_LEVEL}
          strings={changePasswordStrings}
        />
      </section>
    </RequireAuth>
    <RequireAuth client:only="react" allowRoles={['principal-clinician', 'helpdesk']}>
      {/* 2026-09-08: *"the buttons on the dashboard are all look quite
          basic."* Still links — each one navigates, so it has to behave like
          a link on a middle-click and on hover — but drawn as the controls
          the owner has called them since they were built. See
          `dashboard-styles.ts`. */}
      <nav class="ndn-account-nav" aria-label={t('account.patientAdminLink', undefined, locale)}>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <Link href={`/${locale}/account/patient-admin`}>
              {t('account.patientAdminLink', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </RequireAuth>
    {/* 2026-09-06: *"there are three buttons - patient accounts, clinician
        accounts and blog and workshops. Split blog and workshops button."*

        The third link pointed at `account/authoring`, one page carrying a
        blog form, a workshop form and a published-item list for each. They
        are two jobs done at different times — a post is written when there is
        something to say, a workshop when one is scheduled — and the page that
        held both made each of them longer. There are two links and two pages
        now; the page itself is deleted rather than kept as a third way in. */}
    <RequireAuth client:only="react" allowRoles={['principal-clinician']}>
      <nav
        class="ndn-account-nav"
        aria-label={t('account.principalToolsHeading', undefined, locale)}
      >
        <ul>
          <li>
            <Link href={`/${locale}/account/clinician-admin`}>
              {t('account.clinicianAdminLink', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
          </li>
          <li>
            <Link href={`/${locale}/account/blog`}>
              {t('account.blogLink', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
          </li>
          <li>
            <Link href={`/${locale}/account/workshops`}>
              {t('account.workshopsLink', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
          </li>
          {/* 2026-09-07: choosing which published testimonials the site
              shows. A fourth link rather than a section inlined here, unlike
              the patient panels above: the page is a list of every published
              testimonial in full, which is not a panel — and it is read at
              the pace of a marketing decision, not on every sign-in. */}
          <li>
            <Link href={`/${locale}/account/testimonials`}>
              {t('account.testimonialCurationLink', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </RequireAuth>
  </RequireAuth>
</BaseLayout>

{/* One `set:html` block for the calendar island's styles. An island cannot
    ship its own inline `<style>` and rely on it surviving this site's CSP,
    and the string lives in its own module so it is not also bundled into the
    client JavaScript — see `account/calendar-styles.ts`. */}
<style set:html={appointmentCalendarStylesCss} />
<style set:html={caseloadStylesCss} />
<style set:html={accountDashboardStylesCss} />
{/* The patient's own five sections are the same record `patient-record`
    shows staff, so they are drawn from the same stylesheet — a patient and
    a clinician looking at one record should not be looking at two different
    documents. */}
<style set:html={patientRecordStylesCss} />
